@page "/achievements"

@* The badges had no home of their own — they were a card partway down the roster, under whatever
   number of heroes you happened to own, which is a bad place for the one screen that answers "what
   have I actually done here". *@

<PageTitle>Achievements · Arkade Heroes</PageTitle>

<div class="page-head">
    <h2>Achievements</h2>
    <span class="hud">what you've actually done</span>
    <span class="spacer"></span>
    <a class="btn ghost" href="play">All modes →</a>
</div>

@* This used to end "and nothing can be taken away", which is the opposite of how the badges work.
   GameService.PlayerAchievements recomputes every one of them from the roster you hold RIGHT NOW —
   heroes owned, bred heroes owned, a Legendary owned, a Fancy owned, a bracket won by a hero you still
   own — so selling, fusing or losing a hero takes the badge with it. Only Trailblazer was deliberately
   made permanent, and the server says so in as many words at the line that records it. *@
<p class="muted codex-intro">
    Every badge is counted from things that really happened — nothing here is awarded by hand. Most of
    them read your roster as it stands, so a badge you earned by owning something goes away again if you
    sell it, fuse it, or lose it in a death-match. <b>Trailblazer</b> is the exception: being first to
    breed a named set is a deed, and it stays yours even after the hero does not.
</p>

<AchievementsCard />
